c(40, "§8.1; part 8 #1", "product-rule", "§8.1 immediate fix — one purchase per decision; never stack an offer on a purchase: 24 of 182 buyers (13.2%) report a double charge, 13 tied to the half-price offer shown during or after buying; if a discounted plan is shown after a purchase it must replace and refund the first, visibly; remove timers from purchase screens; show plan and renewal period on the confirmation screen and in settings; 'why first: it converts buyers into refund requests, bank disputes and one-star reviews', and a support reply acknowledged 'a huge number of such mistakes'.", "post-purchase countdown offer stacking", "1★-burst", "DOUBLE 26 (13 tied to offer); COUNTDOWN 46; WRONG_PLAN 15; buyers double-charged 13.2%", "product-rule", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["7029621975", "6778267872", "7932137213"], "", "")

c(41, "§8.2; part 8 #2", "product-rule", "§8.2 immediate fix — let people see the product before paying, and make the listing say what it costs: 132 pre-use-wall reviews, 97 never paid; 8 name a real trial as their condition; the description says 'free to use' with prices that differ from the IAP list; a usable free core (a few habits and one challenge) before any purchase screen; a free trial without card details, or a paid trial clearly labelled as paid; description prices matching the IAP list.", "hard wall; mismatched listing prices", "blocked-conversion", "pre_use_wall 132 (97 non-payers); FREE_LABEL 33; CONDITIONAL 8", "product-rule", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["6810306576", "6827257273", "6832829686"], "", "")

c(42, "§8.3; part 8 #3", "product-rule", "§8.3 immediate fix — one billing channel, cancellable where it was bought: E3 unwanted charges 47.7%, WEB_CHECKOUT 19, CANT_CANCEL 34, CHARGED_AFTER_CANCEL 21, OTHER_MERCHANT_NAME 4, TRIAL_SHORTER 8, 8 web buyers unable to get their purchase into the app; if web checkout is used, link it to an account that unlocks the app, bill under the app's own name, put a self-serve cancel link in every receipt, and make ad trial terms identical to checkout terms.", "off-store web checkout with no cancel path or entitlement link", "1★-burst", "WEB 19; CANT_CANCEL 34; AFTER_CANCEL 21; OTHER_MERCHANT 4; TRIAL_SHORTER 8; web no-access 8", "product-rule", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["7621555490", "7674187696", "7627531648", "7678142732"], "", "")

c(43, "§8.4; part 8 #4", "must-have", "§8.4 immediate fix — reachable support and a refund path: UNRESPONSIVE 59, refunds 4 of 64 requests, 26.9% of money-taken reviewers report a support failure; the two refunded quickly changed their tone ('que ladrones no son' — they're not thieves, 3★); an in-app contact route that works, a response-time target, and a no-questions refund for double charges and charges after cancellation.", "no working contact; refunds rare", "complaint", "UNRESPONSIVE 59 / 12.04%; refund 4 of 64; refunded reviewers upgraded 2", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["7879858284", "8036849766", "7932137213"], "", "a fast refund flips the review even for a product the reviewer disliked")

c(44, "§8.5; part 8 #5", "dont", "§8.5 immediate fix — remove any link between rating the app and unlocking content: REVIEW_GATE 13 (8 before using the app), five-star reviews carry more helpful votes than one-star (2.74 vs 0.37), corpus 1.714★ vs public 4.355★; ask for ratings only after a completed habit streak, never as a condition; research: check the store's rules on rating requests against the 2020–21 flow.", "rate-to-unlock", "mixed", "REVIEW_GATE 13; vote inversion; gap +2.641★", "dont", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["6824431033", "6830128790", "7069536244"], "", "")

c(45, "§8.6; §8.7; part 8 #6; part 8 #7", "dont", "§8.6 experiment — advertise the app that exists, or build what the ads show: ADS_MISLEADING 72 (52 buyers), USE_CLEANING 12; run creatives showing real screens and measure refund requests and one-star reviews per purchase, not installs — or ship the cleaning and personality content the ads promised. §8.7 experiment — put the content inside the plan: PREMIUM_INCOMPLETE 38 (30 buyers), CONTENT_THIN 54, the listing still sells printables separately; include printables in any lifetime or yearly plan and measure refund requests.", "ads for absent content; printables sold on top of premium", "complaint", "ADS_MISLEADING 72 (52 buyers); USE_CLEANING 12; PREMIUM_INCOMPLETE 38 (30 buyers); THIN 54", "dont", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["7084713878", "7200379204", "7227200950"], "", "")

c(46, "§8.8; part 8 #8", "must-have", "§8.8 immediate fix — the habit loop itself: DEF_REMINDERS 18 (fire at the wrong time or reset to default), DEF_CANT_TRACK 7 ('unable to mark my habits done'), DEF_BUG_UI 28, FUNC_LIMITED 13 (cannot rename, reorder or count habits); 'reminders that fire at the set time, marking any habit done, editable habits and count-based habits. These are table stakes in the category.'", "reminders wrong; no rename/reorder/count", "complaint", "REMINDERS 18; CANT_TRACK 7; BUG_UI 28; FUNC_LIMITED 13", "must-have", "Very strong", "generalisable", ["6809718942", "7287583575", "7521527537", "6839825405", "7569539286"], "", "")

